---
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Website Terms"
  description="Draft website terms for The OC Events Market."
  noindex
>
  <article class="prose-page">
    <h1>Website Terms</h1>
    <p><strong>Owner and legal review required before production launch.</strong></p>
    <p>
      These draft terms describe general website use only. They are not an event-planning contract
      and do not replace a signed proposal or service agreement.
    </p>

    <h2>Website information</h2>
    <p>
      Website copy is provided for general information. Service availability, responsibilities,
      inclusions, staffing, event-day hours, pricing, and vendor terms are controlled by the
      approved proposal and signed agreement.
    </p>

    <h2>No booking through the website</h2>
    <p>
      An inquiry does not reserve a date, create a client relationship, guarantee availability, or
      confirm a service. A vendor introduction does not create a partnership or recommendation.
    </p>

    <h2>Third-party services</h2>
    <p>
      Vendors, venues, and linked services may have separate contracts, policies, pricing, licenses,
      and responsibilities. The final terms must reflect the business’s actual contracting model.
    </p>

    <h2>Photography and intellectual property</h2>
    <p>
      Temporary editorial images are used under their recorded stock licenses and do not depict
      clients or completed work. The official logo and real portfolio rights must be confirmed
      before replacement assets publish.
    </p>

    <h2>Governing terms and contact</h2>
    <p>
      The legal entity, contact details, governing-law language, disclaimer scope, and dispute terms
      remain owner and counsel decisions and are intentionally absent.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
